 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Tires",
   "text": "I observed that the tires of the vehicle are matched with tire brand and sizes however, I noticed each tires shows 5/32 of tire tread depth remaining. All four wheel/rims are showing miscellaneous curb rash on each tire more evident on wheel rim corners/edges."
  },
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "The exterior of the vehicle was dusty at time of inspection. This can hide minor imperfections. There are minor miscellaneous scratches around the vehicle, normal for its mileage, and most are too small to see in photos. I noticed minor scratches and stone chips on the front bumper."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "I observed that the steering wheel shows wear. There is light wear to the seats. Normal for mileage. I noticed minor dirt stains on the seats. There are minor scuffed marks on the inner door panels The interior trim of the vehicle shows wear. I noticed that the trim and bed of cargo area shows scratches and scuffed marks. The center console shows wear. The carpet shows normal wear and dirty. I observed minor dirt stains on the headliner."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "The fasteners in the engine bay looked generally intact and in place, and hoses, belts, axle boots, and visible bushings appeared to be in good condition. I didn't notice any obvious leaks from the engine and transmission. However, surface rust can be found on some portions of the exhaust pipe, welds, and flanges which is a typical occurrence. I observed a knocking noise coming from the muffler. Further diagnosis is needed."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "I found no issues during the test drive. The engine had plenty of power with no misfires. The transmission function as designed, with no harsh engagement or slipping. The steering was responsive, the suspension was firm, and the vehicle handled well. I hooked up my Scan Tool to the computer system and found no current or pending codes. All of the live data looked good, with no reported issues."
  }
 ],
